From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:36:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 66/79] lanes: a backend names the prompts it holds mid-chunk;
 the fill picker finishes an open chunk before switching

Backend.open_fills (0: any; wrappers copy it) and Stream.fill_open (the backend's word after each prefill_step).
When the open chunks are at the limit, lane_host_fill's pick and the fcfs oldest-long pick take only those, so an
aged prompt no longer begins while another prompt's chunk holds the buffers. flashnext_mia's sliced fill
(TF_FLASHNEXT_FILL=1) declares one: its fillStep refuses a second prompt mid-chunk (PromptBuffersBusy), which
both TP2 ranks treated as fatal at the first c4 burst. The fake's stepped mode takes the same limit; the new test
replays that sequence (four short prompts of seven calls each). lane_host_fill's Share-only tests move to
lane_host_fill_open_test.zig with it.
